LINES 17
   Tomas Lind: Is the sign straight? It's straight. Is it the right way up? It's the right way up. Is it?
   Zeke Torres: Ramp's opening. Coil three always hums before a big push, Tomas. Hum if it helps.
   Tomas Lind: Theo went up this ramp this afternoon. Now somebody's coming down it. Busy ramp. I waved at Theo too early, as well.
   Basil Bramwell: Is that for me? Is that my name? Is that glitter? It's glitter. Hello!
   Tomas Lind: Is the sign straight? It's straight. Is it the right way up? It's the right way up. Is it?
   Zeke Torres: Ramp's opening. Coil three always hums before a big push, Tomas. Hum if it helps.
   Tomas Lind: Theo went up this ramp this afternoon. Now somebody's coming down it. Busy ramp. I waved at Theo too early, as well.
   Basil Bramwell: Is that for me? Is that my name? Is that glitter? It's glitter. Hello!
   Tomas Lind: Hello! Welcome to the Wren. I'm Tomas. I'm Watch. You're not lost. That was the main bit. The rest is extra.
   Tomas Lind: When I came down this ramp, nobody was at the bottom. So I wanted somebody to be. Today it's lots of somebodies.
   Basil Bramwell: Nobody? Not anyone? What did you do? Where did you go? Sorry. Pick one.
   Tomas Lind: I found the laundry. Twice. And a secret for your first week: I failed my first Watch exam. And look. Here I am, on the ramp.
   Tomas Lind: Don't tell Holt. No. Do tell Holt. I think I've finished not telling Holt.
